IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-bodies`
IMPORT `uc3-disability-payments`
IMPORT `uc3-sch1-interpretation`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-interpretation`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-bedrooms`
IMPORT `uc3-sch1-payments`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-payments`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-contributions`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-private-sector`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-social-sector`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 4 Parts 4 and 5 (paragraphs 20 to 25, and 30 to 36 including 32A): the housing costs element for renters in the private and the social rented sector.
-- Tests of layer 1.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text).
--
-- EVERY EXPECTED VALUE IS WRITTEN HERE FROM THE TEXT, beside the assertion, before the file was run: none was copied from what the encoding printed.
-- Amounts are in pounds. Where a figure is a local housing allowance or a rent officer's determination (inputs the text does not give), the test supplies it.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers: the smallest records that let one fact at a time change.

GIVETH A `Accommodation in the Schedule 1 tests`
`uc3 test — ordinary accommodation` MEANS
    `Accommodation in the Schedule 1 tests` WITH
        structure IS `Structure that may be a tent` WITH
            `moveable structure` IS FALSE
            `designed or adapted (solely or mainly) for the purpose of sleeping in a place for any period` IS FALSE
            `caravan` IS FALSE
            `mobile home` IS FALSE
            `houseboat` IS FALSE
        `approved premises` IS FALSE
        `care home premises` IS `Premises that may be a care home` WITH
            `nation of Great Britain in which the premises are` IS England
            `a care home within the meaning of section 3 of the Care Standards Act 2000` IS FALSE
            `a place at which a care home service within the meaning of Part 1 of the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016 is provided wholly or mainly to persons aged 18 or over` IS FALSE
            `a care home service within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 12 to the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010` IS FALSE
            `the premises as a hospital that may be an independent hospital` IS `Hospital that may be an independent hospital` WITH
                `a hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006` IS FALSE
                `a health service hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006` IS FALSE
                `an independent hospital as the meaning is assigned to it by section 2 of the Care Standards Act 2000` IS FALSE
                `an independent health care service as defined in section 10F(1)(a) and (b) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978` IS FALSE
        `exempt accommodation` IS FALSE

-- A payment that may be a service charge payment: forServices says whether it is a payment for services (7(2)(a)); no exclusion and no paragraph 8 condition applies (the calculation is under Part 4).
GIVEN forServices IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Payment that may be a service charge payment`
`uc3 test — a payment for services` forServices MEANS
    `Payment that may be a service charge payment` WITH
        `the payment is, in whole or in part, a payment of, or towards, the costs of or charges for providing services or facilities for the use or benefit of persons occupying accommodation` IS forServices
        `the payment is, in whole or in part, fairly attributable to the costs of or charges for providing such services or facilities connected with accommodation as are available for the use or benefit of persons occupying accommodation` IS FALSE
        `a qualifying loan within the meaning of regulation 2 of the Loans for Mortgage Interest Regulations 2017 was taken out for the purposes of making the payments` IS FALSE
        `the accommodation occupied by the person for whose use or benefit the services or facilities are provided` IS `uc3 test — ordinary accommodation`
        `the payments are separately identified as relating to the costs or charges referred to in sub-paragraph (2)` IS FALSE
        `the payments are made in addition to or as part of any other payment` IS FALSE
        `the payments are made under the same agreement as that under which the accommodation is occupied` IS FALSE
        `facts for paragraph 8` IS `Service charge payment, as paragraph 8 looks at it` WITH
            `the calculation is made under Part 5 of Schedule 4 or under Schedule 5` IS FALSE
            `making the payments is a condition on which the right to occupy the accommodation depends` IS FALSE
            `external cleaning of windows` IS FALSE
            `the windows are in upper floors of a multi-storey building` IS FALSE
            `other internal or external maintenance or repair of the accommodation` IS FALSE
            `the payments are separately identifiable as relating to such maintenance or repair` IS FALSE
            `the payments are payable by a claimant who occupies accommodation under a shared ownership tenancy` IS FALSE
            `any amount of housing costs element in respect of those payments would fall to be calculated under Schedule 5` IS FALSE
            `ongoing maintenance or cleaning of, and the supply of water, fuel or any other commodity relating to the common use of, internal or external areas, including areas for reasonable facilities` IS FALSE
            `provision, ongoing maintenance, cleaning or repair in connection with basic services generally available to all persons living in the accommodation` IS FALSE
            `payments specific to the particular accommodation occupied by the claimant for the use of essential items contained in it` IS FALSE
            `the costs and charges to which the payments relate are of a reasonable amount` IS FALSE
            `the costs and charges relate to services or facilities of such description as it is reasonable to provide` IS FALSE
            `the payments relate to the costs of or charges for providing services or facilities in respect of which payments out of public funds might otherwise be made` IS FALSE
            `the payments are in connection with the use of an asset and result in the transfer of the asset or any interest in it` IS FALSE
            `the payments relate to the costs of or charges for providing food, medical services or personal services (including personal care) of any description` IS FALSE

-- A payment in respect of accommodation: rent (a payment of rent in ordinary accommodation), or a service charge payment (not rent), or neither (a payment of no description).
-- kind: 1 a payment of rent; 2 a service charge payment; 0 neither.
GIVEN kind IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Payment in respect of accommodation`
`uc3 test — a payment in respect of accommodation of a kind` kind MEANS
    `Payment in respect of accommodation` WITH
        description IS `Description of a payment for accommodation` WITH
            `payment of rent` IS kind EQUALS 1
            `payment for a licence or other permission to occupy accommodation` IS FALSE
            `mooring charge payable for a houseboat` IS FALSE
            `accommodation is a caravan or mobile home and the payment is in respect of the site on which the accommodation stands` IS FALSE
            `contribution towards almshouses` IS `Almshouse contribution` WITH
                `contribution by a resident towards maintaining almshouses (and essential services in them)` IS FALSE
                `the almshouses are provided by a housing association` IS FALSE
                `the housing association as a possible registered charity` IS `Charity that may be a registered charity` WITH
                    `entered in the register of charities maintained under Part 4 of the Charities Act 2011` IS FALSE
                    `entered on the register of charities maintained under the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005` IS FALSE
                `the housing association is an exempt charity within Schedule 3 to the Charities Act 2011` IS FALSE
        `the accommodation` IS `uc3 test — ordinary accommodation`
        `ground rent` IS FALSE
        `the payment is in respect of the site on which a tent stands` IS FALSE
        `owner-occupier payment within the meaning of Schedule 1 of the Loans for Mortgage Regulations 2017` IS FALSE
        `the payment as a possible service charge payment` IS `uc3 test — a payment for services` (kind EQUALS 2)
        `the accommodation as it may be specified in paragraph 3A` IS `Accommodation that may be specified in paragraph 3A` WITH
            `the accommodation as it is looked at in the Schedule 1 tests` IS `uc3 test — ordinary accommodation`
            `the provider` IS `Provider of accommodation that may be a relevant body` WITH
                `the provider as a possible local authority` IS `Body that may be a local authority` WITH
                    `nation of Great Britain in relation to which it is asked` IS England
                    `kind of body` IS `another kind of body`
                `council for a county in England for each part of which there is a district council` IS FALSE
                `housing association` IS FALSE
                `the provider as a possible registered charity` IS `Charity that may be a registered charity` WITH
                    `entered in the register of charities maintained under Part 4 of the Charities Act 2011` IS FALSE
                    `entered on the register of charities maintained under the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005` IS FALSE
                `the provider as a possible voluntary organisation` IS `Body that may be a voluntary organisation` WITH
                    `public authority` IS FALSE
                    `the body as a possible local authority` IS `Body that may be a local authority` WITH
                        `nation of Great Britain in relation to which it is asked` IS England
                        `kind of body` IS `another kind of body`
                    `activities are carried on otherwise than for profit` IS FALSE
            `the claimant has been admitted into the accommodation in order to meet a need for care, support or supervision` IS FALSE
            `the claimant receives care, support or supervision` IS FALSE
            `the accommodation is provided to the claimant because the claimant has left the home as a result of domestic violence` IS FALSE
            `the accommodation consists of a building, or part of a building, which is used wholly or mainly for the non-permanent accommodation of persons who have left their homes as a result of domestic violence` IS FALSE
            `the accommodation as a building that may be a hostel` IS `Building that may be a hostel` WITH
                `domestic accommodation is provided for persons generally or for a class of persons otherwise than in separate and self-contained premises` IS FALSE
                `board is provided` IS FALSE
                `facilities for the preparation of food adequate to the needs of those persons are provided` IS FALSE
                `the owner or manager as a possible provider of social housing` IS `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing` WITH
                    `the landlord as a possible local authority` IS `Body that may be a local authority` WITH
                        `nation of Great Britain in relation to which it is asked` IS England
                        `kind of body` IS `another kind of body`
                    `non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS FALSE
                    `profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS FALSE
                    `the accommodation is social housing` IS FALSE
                    `the landlord as a possible registered social landlord` IS `Landlord that may be a registered social landlord` WITH
                        `registered in the register maintained by the Welsh Ministers under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Housing Act 1996` IS FALSE
                        `registered in the register maintained by the Scottish Housing Regulator under section 20(1) of the Housing (Scotland) Act 2010` IS FALSE
                `the building is operated other than on a commercial basis` IS FALSE
                `funds are provided wholly or in part by a government department or agency or a local authority` IS FALSE
                `the manager as a possible voluntary organisation` IS `Body that may be a voluntary organisation` WITH
                    `public authority` IS FALSE
                    `the body as a possible local authority` IS `Body that may be a local authority` WITH
                        `nation of Great Britain in relation to which it is asked` IS England
                        `kind of body` IS `another kind of body`
                    `activities are carried on otherwise than for profit` IS FALSE
                `the manager as a possible registered charity` IS `Charity that may be a registered charity` WITH
                    `entered in the register of charities maintained under Part 4 of the Charities Act 2011` IS FALSE
                    `entered on the register of charities maintained under the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005` IS FALSE
                `the building provides care, support or supervision with a view to assisting those persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community` IS FALSE
                `the building as possible care home premises` IS `Premises that may be a care home` WITH
                    `nation of Great Britain in which the premises are` IS England
                    `a care home within the meaning of section 3 of the Care Standards Act 2000` IS FALSE
                    `a place at which a care home service within the meaning of Part 1 of the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016 is provided wholly or mainly to persons aged 18 or over` IS FALSE
                    `a care home service within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 12 to the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010` IS FALSE
                    `the premises as a hospital that may be an independent hospital` IS `Hospital that may be an independent hospital` WITH
                        `a hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006` IS FALSE
                        `a health service hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006` IS FALSE
                        `an independent hospital as the meaning is assigned to it by section 2 of the Care Standards Act 2000` IS FALSE
                        `an independent health care service as defined in section 10F(1)(a) and (b) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978` IS FALSE
        `the accommodation as it may be temporary accommodation` IS `Accommodation that may be temporary accommodation` WITH
            `the landlord that rent payments are payable to` IS `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing` WITH
                `the landlord as a possible local authority` IS `Body that may be a local authority` WITH
                    `nation of Great Britain in relation to which it is asked` IS England
                    `kind of body` IS `another kind of body`
                `non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS FALSE
                `profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS FALSE
                `the accommodation is social housing` IS FALSE
                `the landlord as a possible registered social landlord` IS `Landlord that may be a registered social landlord` WITH
                    `registered in the register maintained by the Welsh Ministers under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Housing Act 1996` IS FALSE
                    `registered in the register maintained by the Scottish Housing Regulator under section 20(1) of the Housing (Scotland) Act 2010` IS FALSE
            `the accommodation is exempt accommodation` IS FALSE
            `the accommodation is made available to the renter to discharge any of the local authority's functions under Part II of the Housing (Scotland) Act 1987, Part VII of the Housing Act 1996 or Part 2 of the Housing (Wales) Act 2014` IS FALSE
            `the accommodation is made available to the renter to prevent the person being or becoming homeless within the meaning of Part II of the Housing (Scotland) Act 1987, Part VII of the Housing Act 1996 or Part 2 of the Housing (Wales) Act 2014` IS FALSE
            `the renter is also liable to make service charge payments` IS FALSE

-- A liability for a payment. kind: 1 rent, 2 service charge, 0 neither; amount and interval; the three conditions together (TRUE or FALSE); already: already brought into account; rentFree and n:
-- the arrangements provide for rent free periods, and the total number of payments in the 12 month period.
GIVEN kind IS A NUMBER
      amount IS A NUMBER
      interval IS A `Payment interval`
      conditions IS A BOOLEAN
      already IS A BOOLEAN
      rentFree IS A BOOLEAN
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
`uc3 test — a liability` kind amount interval conditions already rentFree n MEANS
    `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation` WITH
        payment IS `uc3 test — a payment in respect of accommodation of a kind` kind
        `amount of each payment in pounds` IS amount
        `how often the payment falls due` IS interval
        `the renter meets the payment condition in respect of the description of relevant payment` IS conditions
        `the renter meets the liability condition in respect of the description of relevant payment` IS conditions
        `the renter meets the occupation condition in respect of the description of relevant payment` IS conditions
        `the payment has already been brought into account in relation to the same or a different renter` IS already
        `the arrangements provide for one or more rent free periods` IS rentFree
        `total number of the relevant payments which the renter is liable to make in that 12 month period` IS n

-- A landlord: 1 a non-profit registered provider of social housing (a provider of social housing); 0 a private landlord.
GIVEN kind IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing`
`uc3 test — a landlord of a kind` kind MEANS
    `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing` WITH
        `the landlord as a possible local authority` IS `Body that may be a local authority` WITH
            `nation of Great Britain in relation to which it is asked` IS England
            `kind of body` IS `another kind of body`
        `non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS kind EQUALS 1
        `profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS FALSE
        `the accommodation is social housing` IS FALSE
        `the landlord as a possible registered social landlord` IS `Landlord that may be a registered social landlord` WITH
            `registered in the register maintained by the Welsh Ministers under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Housing Act 1996` IS FALSE
            `registered in the register maintained by the Scottish Housing Regulator under section 20(1) of the Housing (Scotland) Act 2010` IS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 4, paragraph 20: Part 4 applies to renters who are liable to make rent payments to a person other than a provider of social housing, whether or not also liable for service charge payments.
-- Expected: a private landlord gives TRUE; a provider of social housing gives FALSE; being also liable for service charge payments changes neither.
GIVEN kind IS A NUMBER
      serviceCharge IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Renter whose landlord decides the Part`
`uc3 test — a renter whose landlord decides the Part` kind serviceCharge MEANS
    `Renter whose landlord decides the Part` WITH
        `the landlord that rent payments are payable to` IS `uc3 test — a landlord of a kind` kind
        `the renter is also liable to make service charge payments` IS serviceCharge
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 20 — Part 4 applies to the renter` (`uc3 test — a renter whose landlord decides the Part` 0 FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 20 — Part 4 applies to the renter` (`uc3 test — a renter whose landlord decides the Part` 0 TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 20 — Part 4 applies to the renter` (`uc3 test — a renter whose landlord decides the Part` 1 FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 20 — Part 4 applies to the renter` (`uc3 test — a renter whose landlord decides the Part` 1 TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Part 5, paragraph 30: Part 5 applies to renters who are liable to make rent payments to a provider of social housing, whether or not also liable for service charge payments.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 30 — Part 5 applies to the renter` (`uc3 test — a renter whose landlord decides the Part` 1 FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 30 — Part 5 applies to the renter` (`uc3 test — a renter whose landlord decides the Part` 1 TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 30 — Part 5 applies to the renter` (`uc3 test — a renter whose landlord decides the Part` 0 FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 30 — Part 5 applies to the renter` (`uc3 test — a renter whose landlord decides the Part` 0 TRUE) EQUALS FALSE

-- Paragraph 23: the core rent is the sum of the monthly amounts of the relevant payments taken into account (paragraphs 6 and 7).
-- Expected: rent of 120 weekly (520) and a service charge of 30 monthly (30) give 550; nothing gives 0.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 23 — core rent` (LIST `uc3 test — a liability` 1 120 `weekly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0, `uc3 test — a liability` 2 30 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) EQUALS 550
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 23 — core rent` EMPTY EQUALS 0

-- Paragraph 24: joint tenants. The total monthly amount of the relevant payments of the renter and the others (24(2)); then (3) only listed persons liable: the whole; (4) listed persons and others: (A / B) x C with
-- A the total, B all the persons liable, C the listed persons liable; (5) if the Secretary of State is satisfied that allocating by (4) would be unreasonable, the amount the Secretary of State considers appropriate.
GIVEN liabilities IS A LIST OF `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
      listed IS A NUMBER
      others IS A NUMBER
      unreasonable IS A BOOLEAN
      appropriate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Joint liability for relevant payments`
`uc3 test — joint liability for relevant payments` liabilities listed others unreasonable appropriate MEANS
    `Joint liability for relevant payments` WITH
        `liabilities of the renter and of the others for relevant payments in respect of the accommodation taken as a whole` IS liabilities
        `number of listed persons liable to make relevant payments` IS listed
        `number of other persons liable to make relevant payments` IS others
        `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to allocate the amount in accordance with sub-paragraph (4)` IS unreasonable
        `the amount allocated in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate in all the circumstances` IS appropriate
-- Expected, with total relevant payments of 900 a month (a rent of 900 monthly): only listed persons liable (2 of them, no others): 900; 1 listed person and 2 others: 900 / 3 x 1 = 300;
-- 2 listed persons and 1 other: 900 / 3 x 2 = 600; (5) when the allocation by (4) is unreasonable and the Secretary of State chooses 450: 450; (5) does not displace (3): with no others and the flag set the answer stays 900.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 24(2) — the total monthly amount of the relevant payments for which the renter and others are liable` (`uc3 test — joint liability for relevant payments` (LIST `uc3 test — a liability` 1 900 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 2 0 FALSE 0) EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 24 — core rent for joint tenants` (`uc3 test — joint liability for relevant payments` (LIST `uc3 test — a liability` 1 900 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 2 0 FALSE 0) EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 24 — core rent for joint tenants` (`uc3 test — joint liability for relevant payments` (LIST `uc3 test — a liability` 1 900 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 1 2 FALSE 0) EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 24 — core rent for joint tenants` (`uc3 test — joint liability for relevant payments` (LIST `uc3 test — a liability` 1 900 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 2 1 FALSE 0) EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 24 — core rent for joint tenants` (`uc3 test — joint liability for relevant payments` (LIST `uc3 test — a liability` 1 900 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 1 2 TRUE 450) EQUALS 450
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 24 — core rent for joint tenants` (`uc3 test — joint liability for relevant payments` (LIST `uc3 test — a liability` 1 900 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 2 0 TRUE 450) EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 24(4) — the allocated amount by the formula` (`uc3 test — joint liability for relevant payments` (LIST `uc3 test — a liability` 1 900 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 1 2 FALSE 0) EQUALS 300

-- Paragraph 25: the cap rent. (2) the local housing allowance for the renter's broad rental market area and category of accommodation; (3) and (4): where paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies, the allowances for A and B
-- differ and a single calculation is made under paragraph 17, the allowance is that of the accommodation for which it was lower when the calculation was first made, kept while the same A and B apply, and re-determined on re-housing.
GIVEN allowance IS A NUMBER
      paragraph4 IS A BOOLEAN
      allowanceA IS A NUMBER
      allowanceB IS A NUMBER
      single IS A BOOLEAN
      first IS A BOOLEAN
      rehoused IS A BOOLEAN
      remembered IS A `Accommodation for the cap rent`
GIVETH A `Facts for the cap rent`
`uc3 test — facts for the cap rent` allowance paragraph4 allowanceA allowanceB single first rehoused remembered MEANS
    `Facts for the cap rent` WITH
        `local housing allowance which applies at the relevant time to the broad rental market area and the category of accommodation` IS allowance
        `paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to the renter` IS paragraph4
        `local housing allowance determined under sub-paragraph (2) in relation to accommodation A` IS allowanceA
        `local housing allowance determined under sub-paragraph (2) in relation to accommodation B` IS allowanceB
        `a single calculation is made in relation to the renter under paragraph 17` IS single
        `this is the first calculation` IS first
        `the renter has been re-housed in other accommodation since the amount was last determined` IS rehoused
        `the accommodation for which the amount was lower when the calculation was first made` IS remembered
-- Expected: an ordinary renter with an allowance of 800 has a cap rent of 800; paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applying with allowances of 600 for A and 700 for B in a single calculation, first made now, gives 600 (the lower, A);
-- with 800 for A and 700 for B gives 700 (B); equal allowances (700 and 700) are not "different", so (3) does not apply and the ordinary allowance (800) is used;
-- paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 not applying, or no single calculation, gives the ordinary allowance;
-- a later calculation with no re-housing keeps the first choice: the first choice was B, now A is lower (600 against 700) but the cap rent stays 700; after re-housing it is re-determined: 600.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 25 — cap rent` (`uc3 test — facts for the cap rent` 800 FALSE 0 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE `accommodation A`) EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 25 — cap rent` (`uc3 test — facts for the cap rent` 800 TRUE 600 700 TRUE TRUE FALSE `accommodation A`) EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 25 — cap rent` (`uc3 test — facts for the cap rent` 800 TRUE 800 700 TRUE TRUE FALSE `accommodation A`) EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 25 — cap rent` (`uc3 test — facts for the cap rent` 800 TRUE 700 700 TRUE TRUE FALSE `accommodation A`) EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 25 — cap rent` (`uc3 test — facts for the cap rent` 800 FALSE 600 700 TRUE TRUE FALSE `accommodation A`) EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 25 — cap rent` (`uc3 test — facts for the cap rent` 800 TRUE 600 700 FALSE TRUE FALSE `accommodation A`) EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 25 — cap rent` (`uc3 test — facts for the cap rent` 800 TRUE 600 700 TRUE FALSE FALSE `accommodation B`) EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 25 — cap rent` (`uc3 test — facts for the cap rent` 800 TRUE 600 700 TRUE FALSE TRUE `accommodation B`) EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 25(3) — the maximum allowable amount is determined under sub-paragraph (4)` (`uc3 test — facts for the cap rent` 800 TRUE 600 700 TRUE TRUE FALSE `accommodation A`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 25(3) — the maximum allowable amount is determined under sub-paragraph (4)` (`uc3 test — facts for the cap rent` 800 TRUE 700 700 TRUE TRUE FALSE `accommodation A`) EQUALS FALSE

-- Paragraph 22: Step 1 the lower of core rent and cap rent (equal: that amount); Step 2 deduct the sum of the housing cost contributions; the amount is never below nil (14(3)).
-- Expected: core 550, cap 800 gives 550; core 900, cap 800 gives 800; core and cap both 700 give 700;
-- the element: core 550, cap 800, contributions 96.55 gives 453.45; core 900, cap 800, contributions 193.10 gives 606.90; core 50, cap 800, contributions 96.55 gives 0; no contributions: 550.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 22 — step 1, the lower of core rent and cap rent` 550 800 EQUALS 550
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 22 — step 1, the lower of core rent and cap rent` 900 800 EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 22 — step 1, the lower of core rent and cap rent` 700 700 EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 22 — the amount of the renter's housing costs element under Part 4` 550 800 96.55 EQUALS 453.45
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 22 — the amount of the renter's housing costs element under Part 4` 900 800 193.1 EQUALS 606.9
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 22 — the amount of the renter's housing costs element under Part 4` 50 800 96.55 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 22 — the amount of the renter's housing costs element under Part 4` 550 800 0 EQUALS 550

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 5 (the social rented sector). A scheme: operated and approved.
GIVEN operated IS A BOOLEAN
      approved IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Tenant incentive scheme`
`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` operated approved MEANS
    `Tenant incentive scheme` WITH
        `the scheme is operated by a provider of social housing and designed to avoid rent arrears by allowing reductions in rent or service charges or other advantages in return for meeting specified conditions` IS operated
        `the scheme is approved by the Secretary of State` IS approved
-- Paragraph 32A(2): an approved tenant incentive scheme is one operated by a provider of social housing to avoid rent arrears (a) and approved by the Secretary of State (b).
-- Expected: both give TRUE; either missing gives FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 32A(2) — an approved tenant incentive scheme` (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 32A(2) — an approved tenant incentive scheme` (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 32A(2) — an approved tenant incentive scheme` (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 32A(2) — an approved tenant incentive scheme` (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE

-- A relevant payment in the social rented sector.
-- reduction: the reduction applied by the provider under a scheme; commodity: the amount in the payment that relates to a commodity; officer: a rent officer has determined a lower amount; lower: that amount;
-- notAppropriate: the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is not appropriate to use it.
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
      reduction IS A NUMBER
      scheme IS A `Tenant incentive scheme`
      commodity IS A NUMBER
      officer IS A BOOLEAN
      lower IS A NUMBER
      notAppropriate IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Relevant payment in the social rented sector`
`uc3 test — a social payment` liability reduction scheme commodity officer lower notAppropriate MEANS
    `Relevant payment in the social rented sector` WITH
        liability IS liability
        `amount of the reduction applied by a provider of social housing under a tenant incentive scheme` IS reduction
        scheme IS scheme
        `amount which the Secretary of State is satisfied is included in the relevant payment and relates to the supply to the accommodation of a commodity (such as water or fuel) for use by a member of the renter's extended benefit unit` IS commodity
        `a rent officer has determined that a landlord might, at the time of the application, reasonably have expected to obtain a lower amount of the description of relevant payment referred to the rent officer` IS officer
        `the lower amount determined by the rent officer` IS lower
        `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is not appropriate to use the lower amount` IS notAppropriate

GIVEN liability IS A `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
GIVETH A `Relevant payment in the social rented sector`
`uc3 test — a plain social payment` liability MEANS
    `uc3 test — a social payment` liability 0 (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` FALSE FALSE) 0 FALSE 0 FALSE

-- Paragraph 32A(1): the amount of the payment is determined as if the reduction applied under an approved scheme had not been applied.
-- Expected: a payment of 100 with a reduction of 10 under an approved scheme gives 110; under a scheme that is operated but not approved gives 100; approved but not operated gives 100; no reduction gives 100.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 32A(1) — the amount of the payment determined as if no reduction had been applied` (`uc3 test — a social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 100 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 10 (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` TRUE TRUE) 0 FALSE 0 FALSE) EQUALS 110
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 32A(1) — the amount of the payment determined as if no reduction had been applied` (`uc3 test — a social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 100 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 10 (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` TRUE FALSE) 0 FALSE 0 FALSE) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 32A(1) — the amount of the payment determined as if no reduction had been applied` (`uc3 test — a social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 100 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 10 (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` FALSE TRUE) 0 FALSE 0 FALSE) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 32A(1) — the amount of the payment determined as if no reduction had been applied` (`uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 100 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) EQUALS 100
-- Paragraph 31: a deduction for any amount included in the payment that relates to the supply of a commodity.
-- Expected: 100 with a commodity amount of 15 gives 85; with the 10 reduction added back first (approved scheme) gives 110 less 15 = 95; no commodity amount gives 100.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 31 — the amount of the payment after the deduction for a commodity` (`uc3 test — a social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 100 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 0 (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` FALSE FALSE) 15 FALSE 0 FALSE) EQUALS 85
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 31 — the amount of the payment after the deduction for a commodity` (`uc3 test — a social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 100 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 10 (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` TRUE TRUE) 15 FALSE 0 FALSE) EQUALS 95
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 31 — the amount of the payment after the deduction for a commodity` (`uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 100 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) EQUALS 100
-- Paragraph 32(4): the rent officer's lower amount is used unless the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is not appropriate.
-- Expected: determined and appropriate gives TRUE; determined but the Secretary of State says not appropriate gives FALSE; no determination gives FALSE even if the Secretary of State's flag is unset.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 32(4) — the rent officer's lower amount is used` (`uc3 test — a social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 100 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 0 (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` FALSE FALSE) 0 TRUE 80 FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 32(4) — the rent officer's lower amount is used` (`uc3 test — a social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 100 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 0 (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` FALSE FALSE) 0 TRUE 80 TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 32(4) — the rent officer's lower amount is used` (`uc3 test — a social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 100 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 0 (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` FALSE FALSE) 0 FALSE 80 FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
-- Paragraph 34 Step 1: the amount of each relevant payment (applying paragraphs 31 and 32(3) and (4) as necessary).
-- Expected: the lower amount 80 replaces the payment of 100 when used, whatever the commodity amount (fork U3-F23: the lower amount replaces the amount of the payment altogether); not used: 100 less the commodity 15 = 85.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 34 Step 1 — the amount of a relevant payment to be taken into account` (`uc3 test — a social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 100 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 0 (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` FALSE FALSE) 15 TRUE 80 FALSE) EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 34 Step 1 — the amount of a relevant payment to be taken into account` (`uc3 test — a social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 100 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 0 (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` FALSE FALSE) 15 TRUE 80 TRUE) EQUALS 85
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 34 Step 1 — the amount of a relevant payment to be taken into account` (`uc3 test — a social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 100 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 0 (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` FALSE FALSE) 15 FALSE 80 FALSE) EQUALS 85
-- Paragraph 34 Step 2: the amount of the payment in respect of a month (paragraph 7), for a payment that is taken into account under paragraph 6.
-- Expected: a weekly rent of 120 gives 520; the same with a rent officer's lower weekly amount of 60 in use gives 60 x 52 / 12 = 260; a monthly rent of 400 with 40 for a commodity gives 360;
-- conditions not met gives 0; already brought into account gives 0.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 34 Step 2 — the monthly amount of a relevant payment` (`uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 120 `weekly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) EQUALS 520
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 34 Step 2 — the monthly amount of a relevant payment` (`uc3 test — a social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 120 `weekly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 0 (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` FALSE FALSE) 0 TRUE 60 FALSE) EQUALS 260
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 34 Step 2 — the monthly amount of a relevant payment` (`uc3 test — a social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 400 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) 0 (`uc3 test — a tenant incentive scheme` FALSE FALSE) 40 FALSE 0 FALSE) EQUALS 360
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 34 Step 2 — the monthly amount of a relevant payment` (`uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 120 `weekly payments` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 34 Step 2 — the monthly amount of a relevant payment` (`uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 120 `weekly payments` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0)) EQUALS 0
-- Paragraph 34 Step 3: add together the amounts for all relevant payments. Expected: 520 and 30 give 550; none gives 0.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 34 Step 3 — the total monthly amount of the relevant payments` (LIST `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 120 `weekly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0), `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 2 30 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) EQUALS 550
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 34 Step 3 — the total monthly amount of the relevant payments` EMPTY EQUALS 0

-- Paragraph 36: the under-occupation deduction. bedrooms: the number of bedrooms in the accommodation; shared: regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership) applies;
-- code: 1 no domestic violence; 0 all the facts of 36(6) hold (the victim not living at the same address); 2 domestic violence, the victim lives at the same address and the person is not a dependent qualifying young person;
-- 3 no evidence of a person acting in an official capacity; 4 not a sanctuary scheme; 5 circumstances not consistent; 6 no contact; 7 the victim lives at the same address but that person is a qualifying young person and a dependant.
GIVEN bedrooms IS A NUMBER
      shared IS A BOOLEAN
      code IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Facts for the under-occupation deduction`
`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` bedrooms shared code MEANS
    `Facts for the under-occupation deduction` WITH
        `number of bedrooms in the accommodation` IS bedrooms
        `regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership) applies` IS shared
        `domestic violence has been inflicted upon or threatened against the claimant or a member of the claimant's extended benefit unit by that person's partner or former partner, or by a relative` IS NOT (code EQUALS 1)
        `the victim is not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the domestic violence` IS NOT ((code EQUALS 2) OR (code EQUALS 7))
        `that person is a qualifying young person and is a dependant of a member of the claimant's extended benefit unit` IS code EQUALS 7
        `the claimant provides evidence from a person acting in an official capacity, within the meaning of regulation 98(4), which demonstrates that the claimant is living in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme` IS NOT (code EQUALS 3)
        `the scheme is a scheme operated by a provider of social housing enabling victims of domestic violence to remain in their homes through the installation of additional security to the property or the perimeter of the property at which the victim resides` IS NOT (code EQUALS 4)
        `the victim's circumstances are consistent with those of a person who has had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them` IS NOT (code EQUALS 5)
        `the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity in relation to such an incident` IS NOT (code EQUALS 6)
-- Paragraph 36(6): no deduction where (i), (ii) and (iii) with (aa) and (bb) all hold; (ii) is met if the victim is not at the address, or that person is a dependant qualifying young person.
-- Expected: code 0 gives TRUE; code 7 gives TRUE (the exception); codes 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6 each give FALSE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(6) — no deduction is made because of domestic violence and a sanctuary scheme` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 0) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(6) — no deduction is made because of domestic violence and a sanctuary scheme` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 7) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(6) — no deduction is made because of domestic violence and a sanctuary scheme` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(6) — no deduction is made because of domestic violence and a sanctuary scheme` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 2) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(6) — no deduction is made because of domestic violence and a sanctuary scheme` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 3) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(6) — no deduction is made because of domestic violence and a sanctuary scheme` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 4) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(6) — no deduction is made because of domestic violence and a sanctuary scheme` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 5) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(6) — no deduction is made because of domestic violence and a sanctuary scheme` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 6) EQUALS FALSE
-- Paragraph 36(1): the number of excess bedrooms is the bedrooms in the accommodation less those the renter is entitled to (paragraphs 8 to 12), never below nil.
-- Expected: 4 bedrooms against 3 gives 1; 5 against 3 gives 2; 4 against 4 gives 0; 3 against 4 gives 0.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36 — the number of excess bedrooms` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 1) 3 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36 — the number of excess bedrooms` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 5 FALSE 1) 3 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36 — the number of excess bedrooms` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 1) 4 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36 — the number of excess bedrooms` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 3 FALSE 1) 4 EQUALS 0
-- Paragraph 36(3) and (4): 14% for one excess bedroom; 25% for two or more. Expected: 1 gives 0.14; 2 gives 0.25; 3 gives 0.25; 0 gives 0 (no deduction).
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(3) and (4) — the relevant percentage` 1 EQUALS 0.14
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(3) and (4) — the relevant percentage` 2 EQUALS 0.25
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(3) and (4) — the relevant percentage` 3 EQUALS 0.25
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(3) and (4) — the relevant percentage` 0 EQUALS 0
-- Paragraph 36(1), (5) and (6): a deduction is made where the bedrooms exceed the entitlement, unless regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership) applies (5) or the sanctuary scheme facts hold (6).
-- Expected: 4 against 3 with no domestic violence gives TRUE; 4 against 4 gives FALSE; shared ownership gives FALSE; the sanctuary facts (code 0, code 7) give FALSE; domestic violence without the other facts (codes 2 to 6) leaves the deduction TRUE.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(1) — a deduction for under-occupation is to be made` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 1) 3 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(1) — a deduction for under-occupation is to be made` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 1) 4 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(1) — a deduction for under-occupation is to be made` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 TRUE 1) 3 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(1) — a deduction for under-occupation is to be made` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 0) 3 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(1) — a deduction for under-occupation is to be made` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 7) 3 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(1) — a deduction for under-occupation is to be made` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 2) 3 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(1) — a deduction for under-occupation is to be made` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 3) 3 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(1) — a deduction for under-occupation is to be made` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 4) 3 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(1) — a deduction for under-occupation is to be made` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 5) 3 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(1) — a deduction for under-occupation is to be made` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 6) 3 EQUALS TRUE
-- Paragraph 36(2): the deduction is A x B. Expected with A = 500: one excess bedroom 500 x 14% = 70; two excess 500 x 25% = 125; three excess 125; none 0; shared ownership 0; sanctuary scheme facts 0.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(2) — the amount of the under-occupation deduction` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 1) 3 500 EQUALS 70
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(2) — the amount of the under-occupation deduction` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 5 FALSE 1) 3 500 EQUALS 125
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(2) — the amount of the under-occupation deduction` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 6 FALSE 1) 3 500 EQUALS 125
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(2) — the amount of the under-occupation deduction` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 3 FALSE 1) 3 500 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(2) — the amount of the under-occupation deduction` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 5 TRUE 1) 3 500 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 36(2) — the amount of the under-occupation deduction` (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 5 FALSE 0) 3 500 EQUALS 0

-- Paragraph 34 Step 4 and the result: amount S for a renter alone liable is the total monthly amount less the under-occupation deduction.
-- Expected, with relevant payments of 520 (weekly rent 120) and 30 (monthly service charge), total 550: one excess bedroom: 550 less 550 x 14% = 77 gives 473; two excess: 550 less 137.50 gives 412.50;
-- no excess bedroom: 550; shared ownership: 550; the sanctuary scheme facts: 550.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 34 — amount S` (LIST `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 120 `weekly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0), `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 2 30 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 1) 3 EQUALS 473
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 34 — amount S` (LIST `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 120 `weekly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0), `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 2 30 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 5 FALSE 1) 3 EQUALS 412.5
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 34 — amount S` (LIST `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 120 `weekly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0), `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 2 30 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 3 FALSE 1) 3 EQUALS 550
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 34 — amount S` (LIST `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 120 `weekly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0), `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 2 30 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 TRUE 1) 3 EQUALS 550
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 34 — amount S` (LIST `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 120 `weekly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0), `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 2 30 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 0) 3 EQUALS 550

-- Paragraph 35: joint tenants. The relevant payments of the renter and the others total 900 a month (one rent of 900).
GIVEN payments IS A LIST OF `Relevant payment in the social rented sector`
      listed IS A NUMBER
      others IS A NUMBER
      unreasonable IS A BOOLEAN
      appropriate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Joint liability in the social rented sector`
`uc3 test — joint liability in the social rented sector` payments listed others unreasonable appropriate MEANS
    `Joint liability in the social rented sector` WITH
        `relevant payments of the renter and of the others in respect of the accommodation taken as a whole` IS payments
        `number of listed persons liable to make relevant payments` IS listed
        `number of other persons liable to make relevant payments` IS others
        `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to determine amount S in accordance with sub-paragraph (4)` IS unreasonable
        `amount S determined in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate in all the circumstances` IS appropriate
-- Expected: (3) only listed persons liable (2, no others), 4 bedrooms against 3 (14%): 900 less 126 = 774; with no excess bedroom: 900; (4) 1 listed person and 2 others: 900 / 3 x 1 = 300 (no under-occupation deduction in this case, fork U3-F22: asserted as the reading taken);
-- 2 listed and 1 other: 900 / 3 x 2 = 600; (5) the Secretary of State is satisfied that (4) is unreasonable and determines 450: 450; (5) does not displace (3): with no others the amount stays 774.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 35 — amount S for joint tenants` (`uc3 test — joint liability in the social rented sector` (LIST `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 900 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) 2 0 FALSE 0) (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 1) 3 EQUALS 774
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 35 — amount S for joint tenants` (`uc3 test — joint liability in the social rented sector` (LIST `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 900 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) 2 0 FALSE 0) (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 3 FALSE 1) 3 EQUALS 900
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 35 — amount S for joint tenants` (`uc3 test — joint liability in the social rented sector` (LIST `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 900 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) 1 2 FALSE 0) (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 1) 3 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 35 — amount S for joint tenants` (`uc3 test — joint liability in the social rented sector` (LIST `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 900 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) 2 1 FALSE 0) (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 1) 3 EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 35 — amount S for joint tenants` (`uc3 test — joint liability in the social rented sector` (LIST `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 900 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) 1 2 TRUE 450) (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 1) 3 EQUALS 450
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 35 — amount S for joint tenants` (`uc3 test — joint liability in the social rented sector` (LIST `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 900 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) 2 0 TRUE 450) (`uc3 test — facts for the under-occupation deduction` 4 FALSE 1) 3 EQUALS 774
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 35(4) — amount S by the formula` (`uc3 test — joint liability in the social rented sector` (LIST `uc3 test — a plain social payment` (`uc3 test — a liability` 1 900 `monthly payments` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)) 1 2 FALSE 0) EQUALS 300

-- Paragraph 33: the housing costs element is S less the housing cost contributions; never below nil (paragraph 14(3)).
-- Expected: S of 473 less 96.55 gives 376.45; S of 473 less 193.10 gives 279.90; S of 50 less 96.55 gives 0; no contributions: 473.
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 33 — the amount of the renter's housing costs element under Part 5` 473 96.55 EQUALS 376.45
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 33 — the amount of the renter's housing costs element under Part 5` 473 193.1 EQUALS 279.9
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 33 — the amount of the renter's housing costs element under Part 5` 50 96.55 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Sch 4 para 33 — the amount of the renter's housing costs element under Part 5` 473 0 EQUALS 473
